{
    "_comment": [
        "Copy to claude_usage_config.json (gitignored) to show the CLAUDE USAGE tile on",
        "the monitor page. The file is optional: with no file the meter is off, and every",
        "value below is already the built-in default, so a real config only needs the",
        "keys it actually changes - usually just enabled.",
        "",
        "credentials_path points at the OAuth credentials Claude Code writes for the",
        "logged-in account. Only the access token is read, and it never leaves the",
        "server: the dashboard exchanges it for usage percentages and returns only",
        "those to the browser. The file must be readable by the user running the",
        "dashboard (it is mode 600, so that normally means the same user).",
        "",
        "Claude Code refreshes that token roughly daily. The dashboard deliberately",
        "does NOT refresh it (doing so would rotate the refresh token out from under",
        "Claude Code) - if the token expires, the tile reports AUTH EXPIRED until",
        "Claude Code is run again on this machine.",
        "",
        "cache_seconds bounds how often the Anthropic API is called regardless of how",
        "many browser tabs are open.",
        "",
        "The usage endpoint is itself rate limited (429 with a multi-minute Retry-After).",
        "force_min_interval is the floor between forced refreshes from the tile's button,",
        "so repeated presses serve the cache instead of tripping that limit. A 429 is",
        "honored on top of this: the dashboard stops calling until Retry-After elapses,",
        "keeps showing the last good reading marked stale, and disables the button."
    ],
    "claude_usage": {
        "enabled": true,
        "credentials_path": "~/.claude/.credentials.json",
        "cache_seconds": 60,
        "request_timeout": 10,
        "force_min_interval": 15
    }
}
